 ],
 "equipment_type": "Air handler terminal (dual-duct VAV controller)",
 "applies_to": "Neptronic EVCBM dual-duct VAV controllers (master + slave airflow) with the Modbus module, guide EVCBM Dual Duct-V500-Modbus Guide-180927-ESA.",
 "summary": "The EVCBM is Neptronic's VAV box controller with built-in actuator; the dual-duct version runs a master and a slave airflow loop. Its Modbus RTU module exposes holding registers for room, supply and external temperatures, humidity and CO2 from the TRL wall sensor, setpoints, PI bands, airflow readings and setpoints for both ducts, minimum/maximum airflows, K-factors, balancing modes, motor positions and overrides, TRIAC and analog output setup and the occupancy / mode commands.",
 "transport": [
  "RTU"
 ],
 "defaults": {
  "unit_id": null,
  "baud": null,
  "parity": null,
  "data_bits": null,
  "stop_bits": null,
  "tcp_port": null
 },
 "addressing": {
  "convention": "0-based",
  "note": "The table prints a 'Register Index' from 40000. The intro says the device address is at holding register index 0, the auto-baud setting at index 1 and the port setting at index 2, and those are the rows printed 40000, 40001 and 40002, so the wire address is the printed number minus 40000 (e.g. 40019 supply temperature = address 19). Same layout as Neptronic's TUXB guide."
 },
 "default_word_order": null,
 "firmware": "V500 (guide title)",
 "source": {
  "title": "EVCBM Dual Duct Modbus Communication Module User Guide",
  "doc_number": "EVCBM Dual Duct-V500-Modbus Guide-180927-ESA",
  "revision_date": "2018-09-27",
  "url": "https://www.neptronic.com/controls/PDF/EVC/BACnetModbus/20181001/EVCBM%20Dual%20Duct-V500-Modbus%20Guide-180927-ESA.pdf",
  "pages": "p. 1 (requirements), pp. 2-11 (holding register table)"
 },
 "notes": [
  "Only function codes 03, 06 and 16 are supported; everything is a holding register.",
  "'Scale N' with 'Value x N' means raw = engineering value x N; the multiplier here is 1/N.",
  "The guide's examples are in °C; System Option 1 has a temperature-units bit (Celsius / Fahrenheit), so temperatures are marked °C / °F.",
  "'Master' rows belong to the first (master) airflow loop and 'Slave' rows to the second duct.",
  "Left out: product name ASCII registers 40003-40006; System Option 1 and 2 (40100/40101), whose bit lists are scrambled across columns in the PDF; System Command Status 40103 (mixed command codes and bit states); System Options 4 (40159, all reserved); CL_HT SwitchTimerCount 40146 (range 0-4,294,967,295 s in a single register); Cfg_MixAirDeadBand 40162 (range given only as a reference to other settings, no units).",
  "Heating ramp 2 demand (40043) is printed writable while the cooling counterpart (40040) is read only; kept as printed.",
  "Port configuration codes start at 1 in this guide (1 = no parity / 2 stop bits), unlike Neptronic's newer guides.",
  "Left out by the verifier: CO2 value 40018 (Value x 100, but the range runs up to the CO2 sensor maximum of 5000 ppm, which cannot fit one 16-bit register at x100) and Analog Input 2 value 40017 (0-1000 at Value x 100 with an mV example, unclear whether the range is raw or scaled)."
 ],
